  "keywords": {
    "Acorn": "Play for gold: Acorn {acorn}, Stash {stash}, Great Hoard {great_hoard}. Three of a size combine into the next size.",
    "Spill": "If a summon from this has no room, get an Acorn instead.",
    "Pass": "At End of Turn, this travels along touching units in the zigzag F1-B1-F2-B2-F3-B3-F4, and the last one keeps it.",
    "Ring": "Whoever stands on this slot has these stats.",
    "Rainbow": "A unit played into an empty slot paints it. A band fades if its unit moves or leaves.",
    "Shy": "If this gains Attack or Health on your board during recruiting, it walks out. Gain 2 gold next turn (4 if golden). This is not a sale.",
    "Bristle": "When an enemy deals this damage in an attack, it takes this much back.",
    "Hunker": "Takes half damage when attacked, rounded up.",
    "Hex": "Start of Combat: the enemy slot across from this has less Attack, whoever stands there, for this fight.",
    "Nightshade": "Whenever attacked, this first loses half its current Health, rounded down.",
    "Belly": "Holds this many units, dropped in from the shop, your hand or your board. They wait inside, idle and safe. When this dies they come out alive, last in first.",
    "Fly South": "Sends this away for no sale gold. It returns to your hand in 2 turns, and its When played can fire again. Its slot holds a Nest. Played or landed this turn, a sale is final.",
    "Nest": "The slot a Bird left, until it comes home. Empty, it holds an Egg with that Bird's Attack and Health, and no text. Mother Goose's own Egg stays 0/2. A slot holds one Nest.",
    "Swoop": "Attacks the enemy back row while there's anyone in it, from either row.",
    "Mired": "Standing on a bog patch. While the unit that made it lives, this must attack that unit. Moving off the patch frees this.",
    "Borrowed": "Fights for the other side until it has attacked once, then goes home. Combat buffs stay until the fight ends.",
    "Pin": "An enemy this hurts skips its next attack.",
    "Stalled": "Skips its next attack, then loses Stalled.",
    "Mire": "At the bell, this makes a bog patch in the enemy slot across. Whoever stands there must attack this while this lives, even in your back row.",
    "Quarry": "At the bell, mark the enemy across. This attacks that enemy whenever rows allow. The mark follows the unit. Take: when it faints while this Hunter is on the board, even if both faint together.",
    "Bitter": "After an enemy attacks this, it loses this much Attack for the fight, to a minimum of 1.",
    "Snap": "Attacks the Mired enemy with the most Attack, wherever it stands.",
    "Pack": "When a unit beside this attacks on your turn, this joins it once a cycle. Only the leader takes counter-damage. Put this after its leader in the row.",
    "Pounce": "Once a cycle, after your side damages the quarry of a unit next to this, this attacks that quarry at once, wherever it stands. It takes counter-damage."
  }
}
